`D:test_no_test_module_resolves_the_installed_engine_root@80-85[44]` — retain checkout-root and AST false-positive behavior.\n- `D:split_engine@138-143[52]` — retain the install-mode-independent split fixture contract.\n\n## Consumers and protected prose\nThe module is a direct pytest input and pins `tests/_engine_path.py` plus the root-conftest guard. Preserve the static scanner, allowlist anti-drift assertion, manufactured foreign-root topology, canonical/shadow controls, and all runtime strings/assertions.\n\nAll unlisted prose is protected as concise or load-bearing: lines 48-49; `_installed_root_sites`, `test_the_conftest_guard_is_wired_to_the_detector`, the foreign-`__path__` test, and the canonical-shadow test docstrings; the line-146 `__pycache__` comment; and every other one-line helper/test docstring.\n\n## Preservation and review contract\nCompare immutable `88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:<path>` blobs with the final commit. Parse Python with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`; remove the three allowlisted leading owner docstrings and permit condensation of the allowlisted `C:<module>:before:_ALLOWED` full-line comment region; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining AST to match. Reject changes to inline comments and all other non-allowlisted comments. Preserve runtime strings, assertions, decorators, test data, shebangs, and every directive-bearing physical line exactly. Only adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed.\n\nA reviewer who did not author the leaf must post exactly 4 leaf-linked TSV rows:\n`stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\nBefore citations use `88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:<path>#<stable-id>`; final citations use `<full-final-sha>:<path>#<stable-id>`. Every row must have `after_words < before_words` and all three verdict fields PASS.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The one-commit changed-path set is exactly the 1-path file-impact set.\n- [ ] Only the 4 declared prose blocks and adjacent blank lines change.\n- [ ] The normalized non-docstring AST remains identical.\n- [ ] Every runtime string remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every non-allowlisted comment remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every directive-bearing physical line remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] Every directive remains attached to the same statement.\n- [ ] Every shebang remains byte-identical.\n- [ ] The non-author TSV contains exactly 4 rows.\n- [ ] Every TSV row has an immutable-base citation.\n- [ ] Every TSV row has a full-final-SHA citation.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `after_words < before_words`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `directives_exact=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `semantic-preservation=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n- [ ] Every recorded content/AST verification command exits 0 at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] Gerrit reports `Verified +1` for the leaf commit.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py","reason":"Condense four audited engine-root convention blocks while preserving the static/dynamic enforcement contract."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","ae4d-df34-480d-4c88"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"ae4d-df34-480d-4c88","parent_status_uuid":"5d4ae4eb-7d61-4b06-974c-3be89ce2f157","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"79cf-60f3-7659-4129","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit — engine-root convention delta","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import ast, difflib, io, json, os, re, subprocess, tokenize\nBASE=\"88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684\"\nAFTER=os.environ.get(\"REBAR_AFTER_REF\",\"HEAD\")\nSPEC=json.loads(\"\"\"{\"tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py\":{\"docs\":[\"<module>\",\"test_no_test_module_resolves_the_installed_engine_root\",\"split_engine\"],\"spans\":[[1,32],[52,55],[80,85],[138,143]]}}\"\"\")\nOWNERS=(ast.Module,ast.ClassDef,ast.FunctionDef,ast.AsyncFunctionDef)\nPAT=re.compile(r\"#\\\\s*(?:noqa\\\\b|type:\\\\s*ignore\\\\b|pragma:\\\\s*no cover\\\\b|pyright:|mypy:|ruff:|pylint:|(?:fmt|isort):\\\\s*(?:on|off|skip)\\\\b|nosec\\\\b|coding[:=]|[A-Za-z][\\\\w-]*-ok:)\",re.I)\ndef src(ref,path):\n return subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"show\",f\"{ref}:{path}\"],text=True)\ndef strip_docs(tree,allowed,required):\n seen=set()\n def visit(node,prefix):\n  if isinstance(node,ast.Module):\n   name=\"<module>\"; child_prefix=prefix\n  elif isinstance(node,(ast.ClassDef,ast.FunctionDef,ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):\n   name=\".\".join((*prefix,node.name)); child_prefix=(*prefix,node.name)\n  else:\n   for child in ast.iter_child_nodes(node): visit(child,prefix)\n   return\n  if name in allowed and node.body and isinstance(node.body[0],ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.body[0].value,ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.body[0].value.value,str):\n   node.body.pop(0); seen.add(name)\n  for child in ast.iter_child_nodes(node): visit(child,child_prefix)\n visit(tree,())\n if required: assert seen==set(allowed),f\"missing allowlisted docstrings: {sorted(set(allowed)-seen)}\"\n return tree\ndef norm(text,path,allowed,required):\n tree=strip_docs(ast.parse(text,filename=path,type_comments=True),allowed,required)\n for node in ast.walk(tree):\n  if isinstance(node,ast.TypeIgnore): node.lineno=0\n return ast.dump(tree,annotate_fields=True,include_attributes=False)\ndef directives(text):\n lines=text.splitlines()\n picked=[lines[t.start[0]-1] for t in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(text).readline) if t.type==tokenize.COMMENT and PAT.search(t.string)]\n return (lines[0] if lines and lines[0].startswith(\"#!\") else \"\"),picked\ndef admitted(line,lines,spans):\n return any(s<=line<=e for s,e in spans) or (1<=line<=len(lines) and not lines[line-1].strip() and any(s-1<=line<=e+1 for s,e in spans))\nfor path,rule in SPEC.items():\n before=src(BASE,path); after=src(AFTER,path)\n assert norm(before,path,rule[\"docs\"],True)==norm(after,path,rule[\"docs\"],False),f\"runtime AST changed: {path}\"\n assert directives(before)==directives(after),f\"directive/shebang changed: {path}\"\n a=before.splitlines(); b=after.splitlines()\n for tag,i1,i2,j1,j2 in difflib.SequenceMatcher(a=a,b=b,autojunk=False).get_opcodes():\n  if tag==\"equal\": continue\n  if i1==i2:\n   assert any(s-1<=i1<=e for s,e in rule[\"spans\"]),f\"insertion outside allowlist: {path}:{i1+1}\"\n  else:\n   bad=[line for line in range(i1+1,i2+1) if not admitted(line,a,rule[\"spans\"])]\n   assert not bad,f\"changed base lines outside allowlist: {path}:{bad}\"\nprint(f\"immutable prose oracle PASS: {len(SPEC)} paths at {BASE} -> {AFTER}\")'","dd_id":"immutable-prose-only","dd_text":"Immutable-base AST, allowlisted-span, and directive/shebang oracle passes."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -c 'import json, subprocess\nexpected=set(json.loads(\"\"\"[\"tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py\"]\"\"\"))\nactual=set(subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--name-only\",\"HEAD^\",\"HEAD\"],text=True).splitlines())\nassert actual==expected,f\"changed paths differ: missing={sorted(expected-actual)} extra={sorted(actual-expected)}\"'","dd_id":"exact-leaf-paths","dd_text":"The one-commit changed-path set exactly equals file impact."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","dd_id":"comment-hygiene","dd_text":"Repository comment-history hygiene passes."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" 